# 基础词 Unit28
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-基础词
# 描述: 基础词Unit28核心词汇

{{jacket}}{/ˈdʒækɪt/}}n. 夹克；短外套}}{{He wore a leather jacket to the concert.}}
{{jail}}{/dʒeɪl/}}n. 监狱；v. 监禁}}{{The criminal was sentenced to five years in jail.}}
{{jam}}{/dʒæm/}}n. 果酱；堵塞；v. 堵塞}}{{The traffic jam lasted for over an hour.}}
{{jar}}{/dʒɑːr/}}n. 罐子；广口瓶}}{{She keeps cookies in a glass jar on the shelf.}}
{{jaw}}{/dʒɔː/}}n. 颌；下巴}}{{He broke his jaw in the accident.}}
{{jazz}}{/dʒæz/}}n. 爵士乐}}{{Jazz music originated in the southern United States.}}
{{jealous}}{/ˈdʒeləs/}}adj. 嫉妒的；吃醋的}}{{He was jealous of his colleague's promotion.}}
{{jet}}{/dʒet/}}n. 喷气式飞机；喷射}}{{The jet flew across the Atlantic in six hours.}}
{{jewel}}{/ˈdʒuːəl/}}n. 宝石；珠宝}}{{The crown was decorated with precious jewels.}}
{{job}}{/dʒɒb/}}n. 工作；职业}}{{She applied for a job at the advertising agency.}}
{{join}}{/dʒɔɪn/}}v. 加入；连接}}{{He joined the army right after graduating from high school.}}
{{joint}}{/dʒɔɪnt/}}adj. 联合的；n. 关节；接头}}{{The two companies made a joint statement.}}
{{joke}}{/dʒəʊk/}}n. 笑话；v. 开玩笑}}{{He told a funny joke that made everyone laugh.}}
{{journal}}{/ˈdʒɜːrnl/}}n. 期刊；日志}}{{She published her research in a scientific journal.}}
{{journalist}}{/ˈdʒɜːrnəlɪst/}}n. 记者；新闻工作者}}{{The journalist interviewed the president about the new policy.}}
{{journey}}{/ˈdʒɜːrni/}}n. 旅行；旅程}}{{The journey from Beijing to Shanghai takes about five hours by train.}}
{{joy}}{/dʒɔɪ/}}n. 快乐；高兴}}{{The children shouted with joy when they saw the presents.}}
{{judge}}{/dʒʌdʒ/}}n. 法官；裁判；v. 判断}}{{The judge sentenced the criminal to ten years in prison.}}
{{judgment}}{/ˈdʒʌdʒmənt/}}n. 判断；判决}}{{Good judgment comes from experience and reflection.}}
{{juice}}{/dʒuːs/}}n. 果汁}}{{Fresh orange juice is a healthy breakfast drink.}}
{{jump}}{/dʒʌmp/}}v. 跳；n. 跳跃}}{{The cat jumped onto the table to reach the fish.}}
{{junior}}{/ˈdʒuːniər/}}adj. 初级的；年少的；n. 晚辈}}{{He is a junior employee who just started working here.}}
{{jury}}{/ˈdʒʊəri/}}n. 陪审团；评委会}}{{The jury reached a unanimous verdict after three days of讨论.}}
{{just}}{/dʒʌst/}}adv. 刚刚；只是；adj. 公正的}}{{I just arrived at the office five minutes ago.}}
{{justice}}{/ˈdʒʌstɪs/}}n. 正义；公正；司法}}{{Everyone deserves justice and equal treatment under the law.}}
{{justify}}{/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ/}}v. 证明…正当；为…辩护}}{{Nothing can justify such cruel behavior.}}
{{keen}}{/kiːn/}}adj. 热衷的；敏锐的}}{{She is keen on learning new languages.}}
{{keep}}{/kiːp/}}v. 保持；保留；遵守}}{{Please keep the noise down during the exam.}}
{{key}}{/kiː/}}n. 钥匙；关键；adj. 关键的}}{{The key to success is hard work and perseverance.}}
{{kick}}{/kɪk/}}v. 踢；n. 踢}}{{The player kicked the ball into the goal.}}
{{kid}}{/kɪd/}}n. 小孩；v. 开玩笑}}{{The kids are playing in the park after school.}}
{{kill}}{/kɪl/}}v. 杀死；消磨（时间）}}{{The hunter killed a deer in the forest.}}
{{king}}{/kɪŋ/}}n. 国王；君主}}{{The king ruled the country for over 30 years.}}
{{kingdom}}{/ˈkɪŋdəm/}}n. 王国；领域}}{{The United Kingdom consists of England, Scotland, Wales, and Northern Ireland.}}
{{kiss}}{/kɪs/}}v./n. 吻}}{{She kissed her child goodnight before bed.}}
{{kitchen}}{/ˈkɪtʃɪn/}}n. 厨房}}{{She spent the whole morning cooking in the kitchen.}}
{{knee}}{/niː/}}n. 膝盖}}{{He fell and hurt his knee while playing football.}}
{{knife}}{/naɪf/}}n. 刀；匕首}}{{Be careful with that knife; it is very sharp.}}
{{knock}}{/nɒk/}}v. 敲；敲击；n. 敲门声}}{{Someone knocked on the door late at night.}}
{{knowledge}}{/ˈnɒlɪdʒ/}}n. 知识；了解}}{{Knowledge is power, and education is the key to it.}}
